/*
	RMSTEST 10 — does scaling use the EXACT map area, or the guide's rounded
	area-ratio column?

	Open across three revisions of docs/preview-design.md (Sec.15 item 7b).
	Sec.4 pins scaling to `declared × dim²/10000` computed from the live dim,
	and argues the guide's ratio column is a display rounding. guide:3429 says
	the opposite in plain words — "multiply your chosen number by the area ratio
	listed for a given map size" — so an implementer reading the guide gets a
	different number than an implementer reading our spec.

	THE ARITHMETIC (run this on SMALL, 144x144 = 20736 tiles)
	  exact:        400 × 20736/10000 = 400 × 2.0736 = 829.44
	  rounded ratio: 400 × 2.1                       = 840.0

	An 11-tile gap. Invisible on screen, trivial for tools/scenario-probe.

	READ IT WITH THE PROBE, NOT BY EYE
	  1. Editor: Map Size = Small, 2 players, this script, Generate Map.
	  2. Save As a scenario.
	  3. python tools/scenario-probe/probe_scenario.py <that file>
	  4. Read the "elevation" histogram. Everything at level 1 is what
	     create_elevation raised; level 0 is untouched map.

	  ~829 at level 1  -> exact area. Sec.4 is right, guide:3429 is a
	                      simplification for authors, and the fixture in
	                      Sec.13 asserting 829 stands.
	  ~840 at level 1  -> the engine really does use the rounded ratio column.
	                      Sec.4's central argument is wrong and the scaling rule
	                      needs rewriting, along with Sec.6.2/6.4's tile budgets.
	  anything else    -> report the exact number. A short count could mean the
	                      clump ran out of room rather than a different formula,
	                      so check whether it is near 829/840 or far below both.

	WHAT THIS DOES *NOT* SETTLE: the rounding rule (Sec.15 item 7b's second
	half). 829.44 floors to 829 and rounds to 829, so both give the same answer
	here — deliberately, to isolate one variable. If this comes back 829, a
	follow-up with `number_of_tiles 500` (exact 1036.8: floor 1036, round 1037)
	separates floor from round.

	DESIGN NOTES
	  MaxHeight is 1 so every raised tile sits at level 1 and the histogram is a
	  single unambiguous bucket. One clump, so the budget is not divided.
	  Player lands are tiny and pushed to the rim because elevation avoids
	  player-land origins by about 9 tiles (guide:1169) and could otherwise eat
	  into the budget. 400 tiles is ~4% of a Small map, so there is no shortage
	  of room.
	  enable_balanced_elevation is deliberately ABSENT — it is irrelevant to the
	  count and adding it would change one more thing at once.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
base_terrain GRASS

create_player_lands
{
	terrain_type GRASS
	base_size 3
	number_of_tiles 1
	circle_radius 45 0
}

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>

create_elevation 1
{
	base_terrain GRASS
	number_of_tiles 200
	number_of_clumps 1
	set_scale_by_size
}
